1	//! Handlers for the `/agents/{name}/runs` resource.
2	//!
3	//! A single handler, [`create_run`], serves all three response shapes keyed on
4	//! the `?stream=` / `?mode=` query:
5	//!
6	//! - default — **one-shot**: block until the run reaches a terminal event, then
7	//!   return the aggregated [`RunResponse`] as JSON.
8	//! - `?stream=sse` — **Server-Sent Events**: stream every [`AgentEvent`] as it
9	//!   is produced, replaying any already-emitted events first.
10	//! - `?mode=async` — **detached**: spawn the run and return `202 Accepted` with
11	//!   the run id immediately; the run continues independently of the connection.
12	//!
13	//! # Execution model
14	//!
15	//! Every request — regardless of mode — spawns one **writer task** that drives
16	//! the agent through the [`Runner`] and drains its event stream into the run's
17	//! [`EventLog`](crate::event_log::EventLog). The response side merely *subscribes*
18	//! to that log. This decoupling is what makes a run replayable (one-shot, SSE,
19	//! and the WebSocket/async-replay transports all read the same log) and is what
20	//! lets `?mode=async` return before the run finishes.
21	//!
22	//! ## Per-session serialization
23	//!
24	//! Before the run is created the handler acquires the per-session lock
25	//! ([`SessionLocks::lock_for`](crate::session::SessionLocks::lock_for)) as an
26	//! *owned* guard and moves it into the writer task, which holds it for the whole
27	//! run and releases it at completion. Two requests carrying the same
28	//! `X-Session-Id` therefore queue: the second blocks on the lock until the
29	//! first run finishes.
30	//!
31	//! ## Cancellation
32	//!
33	//! The run's [`CancellationToken`] is cloned into the [`RunContext`]. For the
34	//! one-shot and SSE modes the response side holds a `DropGuard` over a clone of
35	//! that token, so a client disconnect cancels the run. The detached `?mode=async`
36	//! path deliberately attaches no such guard — the run outlives the connection.
37	
38	use std::{convert::Infallible, sync::Arc, time::Instant};
39	
